Bugfix: Restore relative directory symlinks correctly on Windows

On Windows, `restore` could create directory symlinks as file symlinks when
their relative targets contained `..` or referred to symlinks that had not
yet been restored. Listing the restored directories then failed.

Restic now resolves relative targets correctly and restores selected symlink
dependencies first, so directory-link chains work independently of the order
of entries in the snapshot.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/4158
